<title>USA: Cabletron Systems rescinds stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Cabletron Systems rescinds stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.H. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cabletron Systems said on Wednesday that its board of directors has voted to rescind the company's previously announced stock purchase program.</p>
<p>The board rescinded the buyback based upon a Securities and Exchange Commission interpretation that may not offer the use of pooling-of-interests accounting for companies that have bought back stock and then made acquisitions, the company said.</p>
<p>Pooling-of-interests accounting is a preferred method for companies when making acquisitions, a Cabletron spokesman said.</p>
